  "$comment": "HRB-010 language-neutral drift fixture for validate_custom_values (SPEC-EXTENSIBILITY 2.4.2) - the ONE pin holding every implementation together. CANONICAL: platform.validate_custom_values (plpgsql, applied migration ext_06b). Twins owed by their lanes: aidream/aidream/services/platform/custom_fields/validation.py (Python) and matrx-frontend/features/platform/custom-fields/validateCustom.ts (TypeScript); this file is byte-identical in all three directories and a drifting twin fails CI. expect.rejected_issues / warning_issues are SORTED, NON-DEDUPED [key, code] pairs - they pin the code vocabulary AND the issue multiplicity, which bare field lists are structurally blind to. The issue identifier property is `key` on every implementation. Codes: required_missing | unknown_key | type_mismatch | max_length | out_of_range | invalid_option | invalid_format | invalid_reference | too_many_values | archived_field | byte_cap. Row-level issues are keyed on the reserved literal __row__. max_length counts Unicode CODE POINTS (JS: [...s].length, NEVER .length). `is_required` / `is_multi` / `archived` constrain ONLY when they are the literal boolean true. A malformed constraint is IGNORED, never reinterpreted. `limits` is the optional 4th argument (max_custom_bytes / max_keys_per_row); absent means unconstrained.",
